& [SharedToolContract] is one semantic seam
  + [SATA-001] SharedAttentionToolRequest is a strict tagged union over all eleven existing runtime operations
  + [SATA-002] SharedAttentionToolResult is a closed typed union and preserves every operation-specific result
  + [SATA-003] SharedAttentionToolResponse contains profile operation status optional result optional fault and mandatory nonclaims
  + [SATA-004] one public pure dispatch function is shared by CLI MCP and direct tests
  + [SATA-005] the dispatch function performs no IO clock randomness network persistence model inference signing or effect execution

& [Compatibility] preserves the first shell
  + [SATA-006] cantor-shared-attention continues accepting stdin or --input and emitting the same JSON field shape and exit classes
  + [SATA-007] succeeded or buffered exits zero malformed transport exits two semantic refusal exits three and internal failure exits four
  + [SATA-008] serialization failure is an internal fault and cannot be labelled as a semantic domain refusal

& [MachineSchema] is derived and closed
  + [SATA-009] every reachable shared-attention request response and nested form supports JsonSchema from the same Rust type used by serde
  + [SATA-010] request variants nested forms and MCP argument wrapper reject unknown fields
  + [SATA-011] generated input schema requires exactly one request property and generated output schema describes SharedAttentionToolResponse
  + [SATA-012] schemas are deterministic serializable JSON objects and expose all eleven operation tags

& [MCPAdapter] is stateless stdio
  + [SATA-013] a new separate executable exposes exactly one MCP tool named coordinate_attention
  + [SATA-014] each call carries one complete SharedAttentionToolRequest and has a 32 MiB encoded-argument bound
  + [SATA-015] the adapter retains no frame dream or participant state after a call and delegates semantic decisions only to core dispatch
  + [SATA-016] structuredContent is the complete SharedAttentionToolResponse and text content is a bounded non-authoritative summary
  + [SATA-017] succeeded and buffered are MCP success while refused invalid_request and internal_fault set isError true without dropping structuredContent
  + [SATA-018] tool annotations are readOnly true destructive false idempotent true and openWorld false
  + [SATA-019] server instructions tell callers to preserve exact generation digest faults backpressure epistemic labels and nonclaims

& [InferenceBoundary] is between passes
  + [SATA-020] a host may supply the structured successor to a later model pass but the adapter never inserts data into an active token generation
  + [SATA-021] settlement remains coordination rather than external truth and DreamFrame remains non-authoritative imagination
  + [SATA-022] no tool call authorizes a model host provider network external effect or another Cantor tool

& [Acceptance] is measurable
  + [SATA-A01] source manifest seven-fold explosion justification plan matrix and signature verify
  + [SATA-A02] direct shared dispatch reproduces current CLI operation success buffered and refusal shapes
  + [SATA-A03] generated schemas are closed deterministic and contain all operation tags
  + [SATA-A04] direct MCP invocation is byte-equivalent to direct core dispatch for positive buffered and refused requests
  + [SATA-A05] malformed extra and oversized arguments fail before semantic execution with structured adapter faults
  + [SATA-A06] official RMCP client initializes lists exactly one tool calls it and receives the exact structured response
  + [SATA-A07] formatting focused tests warnings-denied lint workspace regression and scoped Git review pass

& [AuthorityBoundary] is adapter_only
  + permits shared request response dispatch schema derivation one stateless stdio MCP server tests documentation proof and local process invocation
  + excludes host registration model calls llama.cpp modification network listener persistence session store cryptographic participant signatures deployment and autonomous effects

